 rookie Cole Knuble scores first 2 career goals in 3-1 victory over Sabres","description":"— Rookie forward Cole Knuble scored twice to help the Philadelphia Flyers beat the Buffalo Sabres 3-1 on Wednesday night.","story":"BUFFALO, N.Y. -- — Rookie forward <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188341/cole-knuble\">Cole Knuble</a> scored twice to help the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/phi/philadelphia-flyers\">Philadelphia Flyers</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/buf/buffalo-sabres\">Buffalo Sabres</a> 3-1 on Wednesday night.\n\n\r\n              Knuble, playing his second career game, scored his first two goals in front of his father, former NHL forward Mike Knuble, who played 1,068 games with five teams.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565230/trevor-zegras\">Trevor Zegras</a> also scored and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3942459/dan-vladar\">Dan Vladar</a> made 27 saves to give the Flyers their third straight win after starting 0-6-3.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2593315/jason-zucker\">Jason Zucker</a> made his season debut following sports hernia surgery and scored for Buffalo. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233889/ukko-pekka-luukkonen\">Ukko-Pekka Luukkonen</a> stopped 23 shots for the Sabres, who are 1-1-2 in their last four games.\n\n\r\n              Sabres captain <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4294163/rasmus-dahlin\">Rasmus Dahlin</a> returned to the lineup after missing four games with an upper-body injury.\n\n\r\n              The Flyers grabbed a 2-0 lead late in the first period after Knuble’s first career goal at 14:49 and a power-play goal from Zegras at 19:17 when he batted a rebound of Matvei Michkov’s shot out of the air past Luukkonen.\n\n\r\n              Zucker’s power-play goal at 19:25 of the second cut it to 2-1.\n\n\r\n              Knuble’s second of the game 3:03 into the third made it 3-1 after he banked in the puck off Luukkonen’s skate.\n\n\r\n              Flyers forward <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697406/tyson-foerster\">Tyson Foerster</a> returned to the lineup after a one-game absence because of an undisclosed injury.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Both teams are in action again Saturday. The Sabres open a four-game trip against the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/wsh/washington-capitals\">Washington Capitals</a>, while the Flyers return home to host the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ana/anaheim-ducks\">Anaheim Ducks</a>.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-22T02:29:07Z"}}